From: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:20:00 +0800
Subject: quirks: add upstream touchpad support for newer devices

Backport the touchpad quirk entries upstream added between 1.28.1 and
1.32.0. Each block is copied verbatim from upstream (comments and
ordering preserved) so they can be refreshed from upstream later.

New devices covered:

  Goodix haptic touchpads  27C6:01E7/01E8/01E9/01EA/01EB, 27C6:0F90,
                           27C6:0F95, 27C6:0F96
  Elan haptic touchpad     04F3:3355
  Pixart haptic touchpad   093A:4811, plus 093A:0255/0274/1336/200F
                           quirks reworked from the old per-system files
  Synaptics haptic         06CB:D024
  Dell pressure pads       0488:108C/108D, 2C2F:0033/0034,
                           06CB:D01A/D01D
  Hantick                  0911:5288 (clickpad announcing BTN_RIGHT)
  Clevetura CLVX S         BT 36F7:5755
  Microsoft Surface Pro 10 / Flex Keyboard touchpads
  Google Chromebook Roric/Rull, Samsung Galaxy Book 4 360,
  Positivo N8460 / VAIO FE15, Wareus B15, Getac X600,
  GPD MicroPC 2, Acer Nitro ANV16-42, EAECIS NL60R,
  HP OmniBook Ultra Flip 14 pressure ranges,
  Lenovo ThinkPad P14s Gen 6.

Only entries whose quirk keys are understood by this version are
included. Upstream entries relying on features that do not exist in
1.28.1 are deliberately left out: AttrTouchpadHysteresis (Framework
13 Pro), ModelCircularTouchpad (Panasonic Let's Note CF-*),
ModelScrollOnMiddleClick, AttrIsVirtual (QEMU/Oracle/VMware), and the
LenovoPavilionDM4/System76 model quirks. Adding any of those as-is
would make the quirks parser reject the file and libinput would then
drop the whole database - the exact failure mode of the reverted
patch.

All 304 quirk sections of 1.28.1 are kept unchanged; this patch only
adds sections.

Forwarded: not-needed (backport of the 1.29..1.32 quirks updates)
Signed-off-by: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
---
diff --git a/quirks/30-vendor-clevetura.quirks b/quirks/30-vendor-clevetura.quirks
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5b6ae2e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/quirks/30-vendor-clevetura.quirks
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Do not edit this file, it will be overwritten on update
+
+# Touchpad is not a clickpad but INPUT_PROP_BUTTONPAD is set,
+# causing libinput to drop physical button events.
+[Clevetura CLVX S Touchpad]
+MatchUdevType=touchpad
+MatchBus=bluetooth
+MatchVendor=0x36F7
+MatchProduct=0x5755
+AttrInputProp=-INPUT_PROP_BUTTONPAD
+AttrEventCode=+BTN_RIGHT
